{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 37, "model_name": "abacusai/dracarys-llama-3.1-70b-instruct", "content": "Fair traveler thou seekest a journey to Japan's shore\nA land of wonder and magic where ancient meets modern lore\nI shall pen for thee an itinerary most fair and bright\nTo guide thee through the land of the rising sun's delight\n\nDay the first thou shalt arrive in Tokyo's bustling throng\nA city of neon lights and sounds that doth never go wrong\nVisit the famous Tsukiji Fish Market at dawn's early light\nAnd sample the freshest sushi in all the land's delight\n\nNext thou shalt make thy way to the Meiji Shrine's hallowed ground\nA serene oasis in the midst of the city's frenzied sound\nPay thy respects to the deified spirits of old\nAnd bask in the tranquil beauty of the shrine's sacred fold\n\nDay the second thou shalt journey to Nikko's sacred hills\nA UNESCO World Heritage site of temples and shrines that fulfill\nThe Toshogu Shrine's opulent grandeur shall take thy breath away\nAs thou dost marvel at the intricate carvings of a bygone day\n\nDay the third thou shalt travel to Kyoto's city of old\nA place of temples and gardens where tradition doth unfold\nVisit the Fushimi Inari Shrine's famous orange torii gates\nAnd hike the sacred mountain's trails where fox spirits doth await\n\nDay the fourth thou shalt explore Kyoto's Kinkaku-ji Temple's golden light\nA serene and peaceful oasis in the midst of the city's busy night\nStroll through the Arashiyama Bamboo Grove's emerald green delight\nAnd sample the local cuisine of kaiseki and shojin-ryori's savory bite\n\nDay the fifth thou shalt journey to Osaka's city of food and fun\nA place of laughter and good cheer where the night is never done\nVisit the Osaka Castle's majestic walls and moat's watery might\nAnd sample the local delicacies of takoyaki and okonomiyaki's savory delight\n\nThus endeth thy journey in Japan's land of wonder and might\nMay Fortune smile upon thee and guid